{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","packSha":"37aa833c651c0a2916023bded1e9a23ae22972cb05e7fd4662a027e773f89d14","packTokens":6790,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":67,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":678,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":907,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":5069,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":8,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"Map each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Replace phone/email-based parts ordering with a self-service ordering portal\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Allow customers to quickly find parts using part numbers, product names, categories, and vehicle information\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Show each customer their applicable pricing and current stock availability\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"Reduce manual order-entry work for office staff\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Give customers visibility into order status and invoices\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-6\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide staff with operational order queues and delivery information\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-7\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide management with basic sales and product reporting\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-8\",\n  \"text\": \"Maintain an auditable history of orders, invoices, customer accounts, and catalogue changes\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-9\",\n  \"text\": \"Implement customer authentication with sign-in, password reset, and account management\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-10\",\n  \"text\": \"Build product catalogue with search, filtering, categories, and vehicle compatibility\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-11\",\n  \"text\": \"Implement customer-specific pricing and price list management\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-12\",\n  \"text\": \"Manage stock availability with ERP CSV imports\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-13\",\n  \"text\": \"Build basket and checkout workflow with delivery date rules\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-14\",\n  \"text\": \"Implement order management with status tracking and staff editing capabilities\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-15\",\n  \"text\": \"Build customer order history, cancellation, and repeat order functionality\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-16\",\n  \"text\": \"Implement invoice creation, viewing, PDF download, and payment tracking\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-17\",\n  \"text\": \"Build administrative tools for product, user, category, and price list management\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"Is the Customer Account Manager role part of the first release?\",\n  \"answer\": \"No: first release has Buyer, Office Staff and Administrator only\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"Does a Buyer see every order and invoice of their company, or only the ones they placed? The Buyer section says 'their company's orders', but the Account Manager role adds 'orders placed by other users'.\",\n  \"answer\": \"Buyer sees all orders and invoices of their own company\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"Which status changes can staff make after confirmation? Can they skip a status, go back a step, or cancel a Confirmed or Picking order?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Forward only, in order (Confirmed → Picking → Out for delivery → Delivered); staff may cancel any order not yet Delivered\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"Under 'where permitted', when may staff change the delivery date or address before confirmation?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Always before confirmation, limited to the customer's addresses and dates valid under the cutoff rule\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"What happens to a customer company's users and open orders when the company is set inactive?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Its users cannot sign in or order; existing orders and invoices stay visible to staff\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"Buyers see all of their company's orders (answer Q-2). Can a Buyer also cancel or repeat a Received order that a colleague placed, or that staff created for the company?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Any Buyer of the company may cancel or repeat any company order that is eligible\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"With no Customer Account Manager in the first release (answer Q-1), can Buyers add or edit their company's delivery addresses, or do only staff/admins manage them?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Only staff/admins manage addresses; Buyers choose from existing ones\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"For an inactive customer company (answer Q-5), can staff still move its open orders forward, create new orders for it, and have invoices created when its orders are delivered?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Open orders continue as normal and invoices are still created; staff cannot create new orders for the company\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must authenticate users by email and password, starting a session and returning the user's role on success.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Invalid email or password attempts must be rejected with one identical generic error and no session token.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"After 5 consecutive failed sign-in attempts, the account must be locked for 15 minutes, rejecting all attempts during that time, and the failure count must reset after a successful sign-in.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Deactivated users or users of inactive companies must be blocked from signing in and from using any existing session, including order submission.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Signing out must invalidate the user's session token.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Requests without a valid session token to protected endpoints must be rejected with 401 and no data.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Requests to endpoints outside a user's role capabilities must be rejected with 403, with Administrator including all Office Staff capabilities.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Buyers must only see orders, invoices, prices, addresses and account data belonging to their own company, with 404 for other companies' records.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Requesting a password reset must send a reset email with a single-use, time-limited link if the account exists, returning the same response regardless of whether the account exists.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Submitting a new password via a valid unused reset link must change the password, invalidate the link and clear any lock.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Expired or already-used reset links must be rejected without changing the password.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"Administrators must be able to invite Buyers (linked to a company) or Office Staff, creating a pending account and sending a time-limited invitation.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"Administrators must be able to invite Administrators the same way.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"Accepting an invitation via a valid link within its validity period must activate the account; expired links must be rejected.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"Resending an invitation must invalidate previous links and send a new invitation email.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"Administrators must be able to list users with role, company and status, assign a Buyer to a company, deactivate and reactivate users without deleting their orders or invoices.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"Administrators must be able to change a user's role between Buyer and Office Staff.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"Administrators must be able to change a user's role to Administrator.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"text\": \"Reactivating a user belonging to an inactive company must be rejected.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 20,\n  \"text\": \"Catalogue text search must match product name, code, part number or brand case-insensitively, returning only active products.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 21,\n  \"text\": \"Catalogue category filtering must return only active products of that category, combinable with search, and clearing it must show all active products.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 22,\n  \"text\": \"Vehicle search by any combination of make, model, year, engine, fuel type and variant must return only active products matching all supplied values.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 23,\n  \"text\": \"The catalogue listing must show only active products with image, name, code, manufacturer, unit, pack size, Buyer's price and stock status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 24,\n  \"text\": \"Opening an active product must show its image, name, code, manufacturer, description, unit, pack size, price, stock status and compatible vehicles, and retired products must return 404.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 25,\n  \"text\": \"Product prices shown to a Buyer must come from the price list assigned to their company, updating immediately for catalogue, basket and orders when the assignment changes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 26,\n  \"text\": \"Office Staff must be able to view the price a given company pays for a product from its assigned price list.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 27,\n  \"text\": \"Products with no price on a company's price list must display as 'Price on request' and be blocked from being added to a basket or order.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 28,\n  \"text\": \"Administrators must be able to create, rename and deactivate price lists, manage product prices on them, and assign an active price list to a company.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 29,\n  \"text\": \"Changing a price list's prices or a company's price list assignment must not alter prices already recorded on existing orders or invoices.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 30,\n  \"text\": \"Stock status must be derived as Out of stock, Low stock or In stock based on imported quantity against a configured threshold.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 31,\n  \"text\": \"A valid scheduled stock import must update stored quantities and statuses for known products and log a successful import with row counts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 32,\n  \"text\": \"Unknown product identifiers in an otherwise valid import must be skipped, other rows applied, and skipped identifiers logged.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 33,\n  \"text\": \"Invalid, missing or malformed import files must leave stock unchanged and be logged as a failed import with a reason.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 34,\n  \"text\": \"Staff must be able to list stock imports with time, status, rows applied, skipped identifiers and failure reason.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 35,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must never send create, update or delete requests to the ERP system.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 36,\n  \"text\": \"Staff opening a product must see imported stock quantity, stock status, last successful import time and price on each price list.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 37,\n  \"text\": \"Basket lines, staff orders or amendments exceeding available stock, or for out-of-stock products, must be rejected with an error stating available quantity.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 38,\n  \"text\": \"The Buyer's basket must persist across navigation during a session, support adding, quantity changes (minimum 1) and removal, show line and subtotal totals, and be cleared when the session ends.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 39,\n  \"text\": \"The earliest delivery date must be computed as the next working day before cutoff or the following working day at/after cutoff, skipping non-working dates, in the configured timezone.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 40,\n  \"text\": \"Selectable delivery dates must be limited to working days within the configured maximum days ahead, and dates outside that set must be rejected at submission.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 41,\n  \"text\": \"A delivery address not belonging to the order's company must be rejected when set on a basket, order or edit.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 42,\n  \"text\": \"Order submission must re-check line availability, stock and price, rejecting and listing affected lines if any have changed.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 43,\n  \"text\": \"Checkout must show a final review page with lines, quantities, prices, totals, address, date and note before submission.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 44,\n  \"text\": \"A valid order submission must create an order with sequential number, order-time prices, address copy, date, note, Received status and a first timeline entry, then clear the basket.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 45,\n  \"text\": \"Orders must not be created for inactive companies or by deactivated users, even via staff creation or race conditions.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 46,\n  \"text\": \"Every order status change must add a timeline entry with status, timestamp and the user or 'System'.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 47,\n  \"text\": \"Order-related emails must go to the ordering Buyer or to the company's contact email for staff-created orders.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 48,\n  \"text\": \"Buyers must be able to list all their company's orders, including colleagues' and staff-created ones, with key fields, filterable by status and date range.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 49,\n  \"text\": \"Opening an order must show its full details including timeline, lines, totals, note and staff amendments to authorized users.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 50,\n  \"text\": \"Buyers must be able to cancel their own company's Received orders, recording the cancellation in the timeline.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 51,\n  \"text\": \"Cancelling non-Received orders by Buyers must be rejected, telling them to contact the distributor office.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 52,\n  \"text\": \"Repeating an order must add still-orderable lines to the basket at current prices and quantities capped to stock, flagging reduced or unavailable lines, without creating an order.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 53,\n  \"text\": \"Staff must be able to list orders across all customers with key fields, filterable by customer, date range and status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 54,\n  \"text\": \"Staff must be able to search customer companies by name or account number and view full company details including addresses, price list, users, status, orders and invoices.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 55,\n  \"text\": \"Staff must be able to edit Received orders' lines, note, address and delivery date under validation rules, and be blocked from editing non-Received orders.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 56,\n  \"text\": \"Changing a line quantity or removing a line on a Received order must record the amendment and email the order recipient the changes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 57,\n  \"text\": \"Staff confirming a valid Received order must set it to Confirmed with a timeline entry, otherwise reject listing failing lines.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 58,\n  \"text\": \"Confirming an order must trigger a confirmation email with order details and any pre-confirmation quantity changes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 59,\n  \"text\": \"Staff must only be able to advance order status in the defined sequence or cancel, with a timeline entry recorded, rejecting invalid transitions.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 60,\n  \"text\": \"Moving an order to Out for delivery must send the recipient a corresponding email.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 61,\n  \"text\": \"Cancelling or rejecting a non-final order must require a reason, set status to Cancelled, record details and email the recipient the reason.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 62,\n  \"text\": \"Staff must be able to submit orders on behalf of a company under the same pricing, stock, address and date rules as Buyer orders, marked as staff-created.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 63,\n  \"text\": \"Orders and invoices of inactive companies must remain visible and manageable by staff, including progressing, cancelling and invoicing.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 64,\n  \"text\": \"Staff must be able to export a CSV delivery list for a given date (default today) with specified order details for non-Cancelled orders.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 65,\n  \"text\": \"The staff dashboard must show counts of orders by status, orders due today, and invoice payment statuses.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 66,\n  \"text\": \"The dashboard must include a count of Confirmed orders.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 67,\n  \"text\": \"The dashboard must include a count of failed stock imports since the last success.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 68,\n  \"text\": \"The dashboard must include a count of failed stock imports in the last 7 days.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 69,\n  \"text\": \"The dashboard must show the latest stock import result including failure time and reason when the most recent import failed.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 70,\n  \"text\": \"Delivering an order must automatically create a sequential invoice with customer, address, order reference, lines, totals, tax and Unpaid status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 71,\n  \"text\": \"Invoice payment status must be computed as Unpaid, Overdue after the configured period, or Paid once payment is recorded.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 72,\n  \"text\": \"Listing invoices must show key fields, scoped to the user's own company for Buyers and all companies for staff.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 73,\n  \"text\": \"Staff must be able to list and view all invoices, filterable by customer and payment status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 74,\n  \"text\": \"Authorized users must be able to download a PDF invoice containing full invoice details and distributor branding.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 75,\n  \"text\": \"Staff must be able to mark an Unpaid or Overdue invoice as Paid with a valid payment date, recording the date and staff user.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 76,\n  \"text\": \"Administrators must be able to add, edit and retire products with specified attributes, keeping retired products off the catalogue but visible on existing orders and invoices.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 77,\n  \"text\": \"Administrators must be able to create, rename and retire single-level categories and assign products to them, hiding retired categories from Buyers.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 78,\n  \"text\": \"Administrators must be able to upload a product image of allowed type and size, replacing the previous image.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 79,\n  \"text\": \"Administrators must be able to add and remove vehicle compatibility entries on products.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 80,\n  \"text\": \"Administrators must be able to create and edit customer companies with specified fields and active/inactive status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 81,\n  \"text\": \"Office Staff must also be able to create and edit customer companies.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 82,\n  \"text\": \"Only staff and administrators may manage a company's delivery addresses, which must be fully visible to that company's Buyers.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 83,\n  \"text\": \"Administrators must be able to view and change system settings such as cutoff time, timezone, non-working dates, max delivery days, stock threshold, overdue days, tax rate, number prefixes, link validity periods, and invoice branding.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 84,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must record creator and last-changer identities and timestamps on key records and expose them to administrators.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 85,\n  \"text\": \"Staff must be able to request a sales report for a date range showing quantity and net sales per product and per customer, available on-screen and as CSV.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 86,\n  \"text\": \"Staff must be able to request a sales report filtered optionally by customer showing order counts and net totals per customer and product, available on-screen and as CSV.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}